WEBVTT

00:02.750 --> 00:04.180
The Temple?

00:04.180 --> 00:05.570
What's that, again?

00:05.570 --> 00:07.150
You forgot that, too?

00:07.510 --> 00:10.800
This is fundamental knowledge
related to nobility and Divine Arts,

00:10.800 --> 00:12.610
so you need to remember.

00:12.610 --> 00:14.080
O-Okay.

00:15.030 --> 00:19.770
The Temple is the largest international
religious group in the world.

00:19.770 --> 00:24.370
It has the role of ascertaining
newborn children's Guardian Deities,

00:24.370 --> 00:27.280
making them able to use Divine Arts,
and granting aristocratic status.

00:27.280 --> 00:28.640
Come to think of it,

00:28.640 --> 00:34.180
Lotte did say something about me becoming a
commoner if I couldn't use Divine Arts...

00:34.180 --> 00:35.690
But that's not all.

00:35.690 --> 00:38.630
It's also the Temple that
selects each nation's ruler,

00:38.630 --> 00:41.380
and gives them their wand and crown.

00:41.790 --> 00:45.360
So the Temple's authority
is above that of the state?

00:45.360 --> 00:48.050
Yes. If they felt like it,

00:48.050 --> 00:54.280
they could probably clash with Her Majesty
the Empress, let alone a duke or archduke.

00:54.800 --> 00:58.240
Special even within the Temple
is the Office of Inquisition.

00:58.240 --> 01:00.710
The... Office of Inquisition?

01:00.710 --> 01:06.370
An organization that eliminates evil spirits
and heretics using Divine Arts for injustice.

01:06.370 --> 01:08.600
The unit under direct control
of the Grand Temple

01:08.600 --> 01:11.200
is said to be a band of ruthless elites.

01:11.200 --> 01:12.220
That's scary.

01:12.500 --> 01:17.730
Don't worry! Normal people will never have
any dealings with the Office of Inquisition.

01:24.720 --> 01:29.020
I am Grand Temple Inquisitor Salomon.

01:29.740 --> 01:33.210
And <i>you</i> are the boy with no shadow.

01:57.470 --> 02:03.890
<b>Parallel World Pharmacy</b>

03:04.950 --> 03:09.910
<b>Episode 7</b>

03:16.460 --> 03:19.890
To be so bold as to run a
pharmacy in the middle of town

03:19.890 --> 03:22.860
and venture outside with
the sun high in the sky...

03:22.860 --> 03:25.170
You left yourself far too open,

03:25.610 --> 03:26.880
boy.

03:26.880 --> 03:27.710
Or...

03:28.100 --> 03:30.810
should I say, evil spirit
in the guise of a boy?

03:31.680 --> 03:33.890
I am not an evil spirit.

03:33.890 --> 03:35.840
Then what are you?

03:36.380 --> 03:39.170
I... would say I'm human.

03:39.170 --> 03:41.860
We need no confession to find you out.

03:41.860 --> 03:44.660
Put your hands up, and take ten steps back!

03:45.580 --> 03:47.870
<i>I don't want to make this situation any worse.</i>

03:50.650 --> 03:52.830
Good. Keep walking backwards.

03:54.530 --> 03:55.930
Bind!

04:11.680 --> 04:13.900
The array that counters evil spirits!

04:17.200 --> 04:19.850
Well, I'm not an evil spirit, so...

04:25.870 --> 04:27.320
Reveal your true form!

04:29.270 --> 04:30.780
Whirling Dance of Flame!

04:36.030 --> 04:37.680
<i>Create nitrogen.</i>

04:39.390 --> 04:40.850
<i>Fire shield!</i>

04:45.550 --> 04:46.470
<i>Good.</i>

04:46.840 --> 04:48.940
<i>Eliminate the oxygen, and...</i>

04:49.350 --> 04:50.560
<i>the fire is extinguished!</i>

04:52.070 --> 04:53.590
What? With no wand?

04:53.590 --> 04:56.070
His attribute is negative fire?

04:56.070 --> 04:57.260
In that case...

04:59.240 --> 05:01.070
Sword Dance of Ice!

05:05.760 --> 05:06.580
Impossible!

05:06.580 --> 05:08.410
He has multiple attributes?

05:08.410 --> 05:10.010
What in the world is he?

05:13.780 --> 05:16.550
As I told you, I'm just a person.

05:16.550 --> 05:20.260
Forget about capturing him alive.
Obliterate him!

05:20.260 --> 05:21.210
Yes, sir!

05:21.210 --> 05:23.160
What?!

05:23.160 --> 05:27.630
Heretics must die!
Attack simultaneously with full power!

05:27.630 --> 05:29.850
Enraged Earth!

05:29.850 --> 05:31.640
Eastern Dragon's Spiral Dance!

05:32.060 --> 05:33.790
Slash of Wind!

05:34.260 --> 05:36.220
Torrent of Fire!

05:45.060 --> 05:46.410
Did we get him?

06:02.120 --> 06:04.840
I had hoped to avoid violence, but...

06:10.890 --> 06:12.240
Divine Power accumulation!

06:12.240 --> 06:13.010
It's huge...

06:13.010 --> 06:13.610
Here it comes!

06:15.060 --> 06:17.000
Defensive Barri—

06:21.940 --> 06:23.380
Commander Salomon!

06:27.150 --> 06:29.360
Wh-What is that?

06:34.570 --> 06:36.790
Won't you call off your attack?

06:36.790 --> 06:40.500
I didn't come to this world to fight.

06:40.500 --> 06:42.960
His body... is glowing...

06:43.750 --> 06:48.630
I would rather use these powers
to heal than to harm.

06:48.630 --> 06:52.570
So, won't you please withdraw?

06:53.500 --> 06:55.110
That mark...

06:55.480 --> 07:02.060
Endless Divine Power, a shadow-less body,
and the holy mark of the Panactheos...

07:02.060 --> 07:03.460
Commander Salomon?

07:03.460 --> 07:06.520
With these things right in front of me,

07:06.520 --> 07:08.980
how could I have missed it?

07:09.320 --> 07:14.140
The vessel has no shadow,
for the being itself is light.

07:14.140 --> 07:14.950
In other words,

07:15.190 --> 07:18.160
the individual before us is the Panactheos!

07:18.410 --> 07:19.260
Huh?!

07:19.630 --> 07:20.610
Wha—

07:20.610 --> 07:24.460
That means... we raised our wands
against a Guardian Deity...

07:24.460 --> 07:26.920
No, no. I'm not a—

07:26.920 --> 07:28.060
O Panactheos,

07:28.060 --> 07:29.330
Uh, yes?

07:29.330 --> 07:34.560
This must be divine punishment
for my great sin.

07:35.090 --> 07:37.800
When I fell from my horse earlier...

07:39.260 --> 07:41.020
C-Commander Salomon!

07:41.020 --> 07:45.140
This wound will likely result
in my death sooner or later.

07:45.140 --> 07:48.960
Before that happens, I beg you,
allow me to atone with my life.

07:48.960 --> 07:50.230
H-Hold on!

07:50.490 --> 07:56.450
Please, let my life suffice to quell your
indignation at our blasphemous acts.

07:57.970 --> 08:00.630
O Panactheos, please forgive us.

08:00.630 --> 08:01.280
Stop!

08:09.960 --> 08:14.960
I told you. I don't wish
for anyone to be harmed!

08:14.960 --> 08:18.470
All I ask is that you leave me
and my pharmacy alone!

08:18.470 --> 08:20.900
There's no need for anyone to die!

08:24.140 --> 08:27.730
<i>His upper shin is fractured,
and blood is coming from the skin.</i>

08:27.730 --> 08:31.820
<i>Taking the fall from his horse
into account... an open fracture!</i>

08:32.820 --> 08:35.520
<i>A white glow... Recovery is possible.</i>

08:35.890 --> 08:38.180
<i>Treatment: Lower leg amputation.</i>

08:40.180 --> 08:41.710
<i>A red glow?</i>

08:41.710 --> 08:42.960
<i>What's going on?</i>

08:42.960 --> 08:47.780
<i>If I amputate, it'll cause an infection
leading to sepsis and death? Is that it?</i>

08:48.080 --> 08:49.460
<i>In that case...</i>

08:49.750 --> 08:51.690
<i>Treatment: reduction.</i>

08:55.410 --> 08:57.150
<i>So that's the solution.</i>

08:57.580 --> 09:00.940
<i>But, who should perform the operation?</i>

09:10.590 --> 09:12.190
<i>I'm a pharmaceutist.</i>

09:12.190 --> 09:14.380
<i>Surgical procedures aren't my forte.</i>

09:14.700 --> 09:19.710
<i>But can this operation be left
to one of this world's doctors?</i>

09:22.370 --> 09:25.430
<i>Even in Novalout College's latest data,</i>

09:25.430 --> 09:27.460
<i>surgery outcomes are practically
a matter of chance.</i>

09:27.460 --> 09:31.650
<i>And the risk of infection can only be kept
low in the first six hours from injury.</i>

09:31.950 --> 09:34.420
<i>His best chance is to be treated right away.</i>

09:34.420 --> 09:35.590
<i>That means...</i>

09:37.370 --> 09:41.370
All of you, please forget
everything you're about to see.

09:41.370 --> 09:42.310
What do you...

09:48.350 --> 09:50.520
I'm providing emergency first aid.

09:50.520 --> 09:52.460
Place the patient up here.

09:52.460 --> 09:54.930
And send someone for a carriage!

09:54.930 --> 09:56.230
A-At once!

09:56.590 --> 10:00.190
Why are you not punishing our transgression?

10:00.190 --> 10:01.690
Never mind that right now!

10:02.070 --> 10:05.750
Don't concern yourself with
anything but your injury.

10:16.150 --> 10:19.300
I will now treat your bone fracture.

10:19.740 --> 10:23.040
First, I'll have you take antibiotics
to prevent infection.

10:23.040 --> 10:25.390
Then I'll inject your back with anesthesia.

10:25.390 --> 10:28.290
Then comes a thorough cleaning of the wound,

10:28.290 --> 10:31.340
and then I'll cut out foreign
matter and contaminated tissue.

10:31.690 --> 10:34.400
Finally, I'll stitch the wound
with thread and bandage it,

10:34.400 --> 10:37.480
so as to move you elsewhere to
conduct fixation of the fracture.

10:38.390 --> 10:39.780
May I begin?

10:40.110 --> 10:43.470
Do as you wish, O Guardian Deity.

10:49.310 --> 10:50.730
Spinal anesthesia.

10:51.100 --> 10:54.090
I'm injecting bupivacaine
into your spinal cord.

10:55.250 --> 10:57.040
Grit your teeth and bear it.

11:11.120 --> 11:14.240
How does this feel? Is it cold? Any pain?

11:14.240 --> 11:17.720
It's as if I'm being
touched through clothing.

11:17.720 --> 11:20.200
And I can't feel any pain anymore...

11:20.730 --> 11:23.790
Is this one of the miraculous
feats of a Guardian Deity?

11:27.480 --> 11:31.410
<i>I've conducted numerous
surgeries on lab animals.</i>

11:33.220 --> 11:36.500
<i>If I do nothing, he'll die for certain.</i>

11:37.180 --> 11:39.300
<i>It's not about being a
pharmaceutist or a physician!</i>

11:39.300 --> 11:42.120
<i>Right now, there's no one else but me!</i>

11:46.100 --> 11:47.520
Panactheos!

11:51.610 --> 11:55.350
I can't say how much the
emergency procedure will do.

11:59.320 --> 12:02.520
But for now, your commander
is in good shape.

12:03.760 --> 12:06.240
Please take him to the Temple.

12:06.240 --> 12:10.270
I'll come check on him later
and take appropriate measures.

12:10.270 --> 12:14.260
To not only spare us your punishment
but even show us such benevolence...

12:14.260 --> 12:15.980
How can we ever thank you?

12:15.980 --> 12:17.490
Don't worry about that.

12:17.490 --> 12:20.000
As one who pursues the path of medicine,

12:20.000 --> 12:21.580
and as a human being,

12:21.580 --> 12:23.960
I chose to do the most good I could.

12:24.510 --> 12:25.730
Nothing more.

12:26.800 --> 12:30.530
More importantly, please keep this
between yourselves.

12:32.730 --> 12:35.620
As the Panactheos commands.

12:42.990 --> 12:46.990
Several Months Later

12:46.990 --> 12:52.210
The new bishop is personally
making a courtesy visit?!

12:52.210 --> 12:55.410
My name is Salomon. A pleasure
to make your acquaintance.

12:55.750 --> 12:58.220
Please, accept this gift
and enjoy it together.

13:02.060 --> 13:04.070
You are too kind!

13:04.070 --> 13:05.550
You're looking well.

13:07.510 --> 13:11.520
Thanks to you. I humbly apologize
for the trouble I caused.

13:11.520 --> 13:13.970
Words fail to capture the gratitude I feel.

13:13.970 --> 13:16.150
It's fine. Really.

13:16.430 --> 13:20.450
From an inquisitor, to bishop
of the imperial capital's diocese...

13:20.450 --> 13:22.580
I take it you've moved up?

13:22.580 --> 13:23.420
Yes.

13:23.420 --> 13:25.950
In order to be of service to you,

13:25.950 --> 13:28.160
I went through countless procedures

13:28.550 --> 13:30.860
and was invested with this position.

13:32.760 --> 13:35.200
<i>I won't ask what that entailed...</i>

13:35.200 --> 13:39.940
Upon taking my post, I sent a
report to the Grand Temple.

13:39.940 --> 13:43.510
It read: "No evidence of heretics
in the Saint Fleuve Diocese."

13:45.120 --> 13:49.880
There was never any boy
with no shadow to begin with.

13:50.180 --> 13:52.850
I appreciate that, but...

13:52.850 --> 13:57.300
In the future, should there be any
reports of such baseless claims,

13:57.300 --> 13:59.020
I, as bishop,

13:59.380 --> 14:02.720
shall take care of it.

14:05.600 --> 14:07.860
<i>Yikes! He's frightening!</i>

14:09.830 --> 14:13.540
Um... I have to say, your retinue....

14:14.330 --> 14:19.680
seems a bit excessive for a courtesy visit.

14:20.520 --> 14:23.140
Might I have a moment of your time?

14:25.090 --> 14:27.090
Closed for Lunch

14:27.100 --> 14:29.530
Where should I enjoy this treat?

14:31.210 --> 14:32.260
Oh?

14:32.710 --> 14:35.640
Miss Blanche, what brings you here?

14:35.640 --> 14:39.520
Brother promised me an
outing with him today!

14:42.410 --> 14:44.350
What's in your hands?

14:48.830 --> 14:51.780
This is not intended to serve as
an apology for the other day.

14:51.780 --> 14:55.000
But I did bring a wand
worthy of your stature.

14:56.130 --> 14:57.190
What is <i>this</i>?

14:57.190 --> 15:01.960
One of the treasures kept in the Guardian
Deity Temple, the Panac-rhabdos.

15:01.960 --> 15:03.960
In addition to the four attributes,

15:03.960 --> 15:08.490
it is suited to combat, diagnostic,
and healing Divine Arts.

15:08.910 --> 15:12.680
It can be freely collapsed and extended,
making it easily portable.

15:12.680 --> 15:15.130
Why, it's beautiful...

15:15.130 --> 15:18.750
Are you sure it's okay for me
to use something so valuable?

15:18.750 --> 15:22.970
Yes. In fact, I'm sure the wand
would appreciate it as well.

15:22.970 --> 15:27.650
But what if it gets broken or stolen?

15:27.650 --> 15:30.330
Try picking it up. You'll see.

15:31.950 --> 15:33.100
All right, then.

15:43.940 --> 15:45.280
What's happening?

15:45.590 --> 15:47.500
That emanation of holy light!

15:47.500 --> 15:50.250
The Panac-rhabdos has acknowledged you!

15:50.250 --> 15:51.100
What?!

15:51.100 --> 15:52.810
It's so pretty!

15:52.810 --> 15:55.750
I'm spellbound just looking at it.

15:57.300 --> 15:58.470
Wanna hold it?

15:58.470 --> 15:59.250
What?

15:59.250 --> 16:00.440
Can I?

16:03.310 --> 16:05.600
Then... just for a little bit.

16:13.250 --> 16:15.290
Wh-What just happened?

16:15.290 --> 16:18.270
The Panac-rhabdos is not of this world.

16:18.740 --> 16:22.460
Only Guardian Deities, who are also not
of this world, can wield such things.

16:22.850 --> 16:24.920
Human hands cannot touch them.

16:24.920 --> 16:28.120
Oh? So then, Farma really is the...

16:28.120 --> 16:33.710
Not you too, Elen!
Stop treating me like a god!

16:33.710 --> 16:34.930
Huh?

16:38.930 --> 16:42.310
Would this wand happen to float?

16:42.310 --> 16:44.270
A keen insight.

16:44.610 --> 16:46.850
This is what the legends state:

16:46.850 --> 16:51.240
If one provides Divine Power
at levels beyond human capability...

16:51.590 --> 16:53.190
I-It worked!

16:53.190 --> 16:56.400
I've never heard of using
a Divine Wand to fly!

16:56.400 --> 16:58.860
This is amazing, Farma!

16:58.860 --> 17:02.970
You are truly worthy of possessing this wand.

17:02.970 --> 17:04.590
Please make use of it.

17:05.490 --> 17:08.540
Thank you, Salomon.

17:13.470 --> 17:15.820
Thank you for seeing me today.

17:15.820 --> 17:16.670
Don't mention it.

17:18.120 --> 17:23.360
The Temple here will visit no harm upon you.

17:23.360 --> 17:27.560
I cannot say the same for whoever drove
that carriage into your pharmacy, though.

17:29.280 --> 17:33.960
Right. It still hasn't been
determined who did that.

17:33.960 --> 17:38.750
A befitting punishment shall eventually
befall those who act against a god.

17:38.750 --> 17:41.360
I keep telling you, I'm just a pharmaceutist.

17:41.360 --> 17:42.750
I am aware.

17:43.100 --> 17:46.800
Now then, please accept this as well.

17:47.460 --> 17:48.590
What is it?

17:48.590 --> 17:51.050
A talisman that suppresses Divine Power.

17:51.050 --> 17:52.370
What? You mean...

17:54.100 --> 17:58.540
If you keep that on your person, you can
conceal your inconvenient disposition.

17:58.540 --> 18:02.000
Thank you so much!
Wow! This is fantastic!

18:02.420 --> 18:06.480
You seem far happier about
this than the wand.

18:07.720 --> 18:09.410
Do I?

18:21.030 --> 18:23.160
Hello, Brother!

18:27.350 --> 18:32.710
I always longed to walk beneath the sun
in the same way they do, alongside them.

18:34.240 --> 18:35.610
I see.

18:38.110 --> 18:40.380
Brother! Come see! Come see!

18:40.380 --> 18:42.830
What a big melon! I wanna eat it!

18:42.830 --> 18:46.570
Melons aren't quite in season yet,
so I don't think it will be very sweet.

18:46.570 --> 18:48.660
Aw... Then, I want grapes...

18:48.660 --> 18:50.530
Brother, buy me some!

18:50.860 --> 18:51.980
Of course.

18:51.980 --> 18:55.430
Master Farma, these apples
look tasty as well.

18:55.430 --> 18:57.880
The plums are fresh and just arrived today!

18:57.880 --> 19:01.190
Then, in addition to the grapes and apples,
we'll take some plums.

19:03.650 --> 19:04.900
Brother?

19:05.620 --> 19:08.070
Master Farma, are you tired?

19:08.070 --> 19:12.030
No, no. Sorry. Where are
we going next, again?

19:16.970 --> 19:19.850
<i>My troubles with the Office
of Inquisition are over,</i>

19:19.850 --> 19:21.930
<i>and my number of customers is only growing.</i>

19:21.930 --> 19:24.880
<i>It might be time to hire some employees.</i>

19:22.340 --> 19:23.850
Brother!

19:24.880 --> 19:28.490
<i>But it's hard to acquire
aristocratic pharmaceutists,</i>

19:28.490 --> 19:32.430
<i>and the experienced commoner
pharmaceutists all belong to the Guild.</i>

19:32.430 --> 19:33.520
<i>What do I do?</i>

19:33.520 --> 19:34.890
Really?

19:35.610 --> 19:39.320
You don't sell any of the medicines from
Parallel World Pharmacy here either?

19:39.610 --> 19:42.450
It's always so crowded there.
I'd love to come here.

19:42.450 --> 19:44.950
Why don't you carry any of those products?

19:44.950 --> 19:47.000
I'm afraid we just can't, ma'am.

19:47.230 --> 19:49.830
Besides, that place is heretical.

19:49.830 --> 19:53.360
They have all these unheard-of new
medicines, and at rock-bottom prices?

19:53.360 --> 19:55.230
It can't get any fishier than that!

19:55.230 --> 19:57.930
But they have a great reputation
throughout the capital.

19:57.930 --> 20:00.710
I am aware of their medicine's
reputation for effectiveness.

20:00.710 --> 20:02.030
Sir...

20:02.030 --> 20:04.190
Mr. Pierre! So then...

20:04.520 --> 20:09.330
Nevertheless, since a son of the Chief
Royal Pharmaceutist runs the place,

20:09.330 --> 20:14.040
there is still the possibility that he's buying
reputation as part of some aristocratic game.

20:14.040 --> 20:15.450
Don't be ridiculous!

20:15.870 --> 20:20.890
Even if they <i>are</i> effective,
as long as the Guild refuses approval,

20:20.890 --> 20:23.510
we can't deal in those medicines.

20:24.080 --> 20:28.010
There are no other guilds in the capital
for a commoner pharmaceutist to join.

20:28.010 --> 20:30.290
I can't defy the policies of the Guild.

20:30.290 --> 20:31.890
This is exasperating.

20:31.890 --> 20:34.510
Medicine-sellers are so
conservative and stubborn!

20:34.510 --> 20:37.210
I'm sorry, ma'am.

20:37.210 --> 20:41.220
Brother, all done shopping! Let's go home!

20:41.220 --> 20:44.120
All right. Shall we all have tea together?

20:49.210 --> 20:52.530
<i>They're restrained by the Guild...</i>

20:55.550 --> 20:58.530
You want to establish a separate guild?

20:58.530 --> 21:02.000
Yes. It'd be nice if there
were a Compounders' Guild,

21:02.000 --> 21:04.820
so the commoners could
sell the new medicines.

21:04.820 --> 21:07.570
Do you know of any stores that would join?

21:07.570 --> 21:10.990
I guess we'd start with ours
and Médique, for now.

21:10.990 --> 21:16.460
Well, two stores <i>is </i>enough to create one,
according to the regulations.

21:16.690 --> 21:20.070
Once we start a guild, I'm sure
other stores will want to join.

21:20.070 --> 21:23.120
Even if it's only the outline,
I'd like to get started.

21:23.450 --> 21:26.680
Lord Cédric, could you help me
with the paperwork?

21:26.680 --> 21:29.020
Of course, Master Farma!

21:29.020 --> 21:31.010
I hope it gets approved.

21:31.010 --> 21:35.470
If we have more partners, we can
reduce the crowding at the store.

21:35.470 --> 21:37.950
Hopefully it lessens the workload, too.

21:38.340 --> 21:40.640
Oh, you sound pretty concerned about that.

21:41.630 --> 21:46.080
How do I put it? I guess I don't want
to accidentally overwork myself.

21:46.080 --> 21:50.620
Listen to you, Farma!
You sound like a 40-year-old man!

21:54.780 --> 21:57.280
Marie! Marie, hang in there!

